{
  "esm": "1.0.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "Spike7aParent",
    "description": "PLAN.md step 7a, the parent half, in the ONE spelling that evaluates. This document holds no model of its own: only document-level configuration — two `data_sources`, the two metaparameters their `extent` binds, the two index sets those metaparameters size — and a single top-level `models` entry that is a `{ref}`. `age_group_census.esm` supplies every variable, every equation and every data BINDING; nothing here names a column or an arithmetic operation.\n\nWHAT 7a ESTABLISHES. A variable declared inside a ref'd child CAN carry `update: {kind: \"data\", source: \"X\"}` where `data_sources.X` is declared only in the mounting document. That is §7.1's load-bearing assumption and it holds: the two Parquet files are read, the equi-join runs, and the numbers are the default database's own (41 categories in 7 groups, ageIDs summing to 820, group 2099 holding 21). The child fails alone with `invalid type: string \"n_spike_agecategory\", expected i64` and evaluates through this parent, which is §7.2's probe carried the one step further that §7.5 said was missing.\n\nTHREE THINGS §7.2 DID NOT SAY, each measured here and filed.\n\n1. THE PARENT MUST RESTATE THE CHILD'S `index_sets`. §7.2 says the fixture closes the shape by supplying `data_sources` and `metaparameters`; that is enough for `esm validate` and not enough to evaluate. Without the two entries below, `esm validate` PASSES and the build fails with `aggregate range 'g' references index set 'spike_agegroup_rows', which is not declared in the document index_sets registry`. The interpreter's registry is `file.index_sets` — this document's own — and a mounted child's do not enter it. Finding F46.\n\n2. THIS DOCUMENT MAY NOT HOLD A MODEL OF ITS OWN. Add one — an asserting model, in the F21 shape, doing nothing but `parentTotalAge = AgeGroupCensus.totalAge` — and every assertion in the document errors with `document holds several models; pass model_name`. The ingesting build takes exactly one model and `--model` narrows the report without reaching the build. Finding F45. So the mount is the whole of `models`, and per-fixture assertions cannot be inline.\n\n3. A MOUNTED CHILD'S OWN `metaparameters` DO NOT MERGE UP, but its `data_sources` DO. Measured both ways: with the extent metaparameter declared only in the child, loading fails `[metaparameter_unbound] … references unbound name(s) n_spike_agegroup`; with the `data_sources` entry in the child and the metaparameter here, it reads and evaluates. That is what lets a shared domain document carry the whole default-database catalogue while each fixture carries only the metaparameter and index-set declarations plus its own runspec sources. Finding F46's second half.\n\nTHE PATH IS ABSOLUTE AND MACHINE-LOCAL, deliberately. The default database is 1.1 GB and is not in this repository, so a `url_template` naming it cannot be repository-relative the way a snapshot path can. run-tests.sh SKIPS the spike stage when the directory is absent rather than failing it, which is how the fixture stage already treats a missing snapshot corpus.\n\nHOW THIS IS CHECKED. `run-tests.sh` emits this document's relation with `simulate --format csv` and diffs it against `expected/age_group_census.csv`, which is the fixture stage's own emit-and-compare pattern and the only verification F45 leaves available. It also asserts that `esm test` on this file finds ZERO assertions, so the day a mounted child's inline tests do run (finding F47) the suite says so instead of the diff silently remaining the weaker check.",
    "authors": ["EarthSciML Authors and Contributors"],
    "tags": ["moves", "spike", "phase7", "run"]
  },

  "data_sources": {
    "spike_agecategory": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": { "url_template": "file:///scratch/ctessum/movesdb/movesdb20241112/AgeCategory.parquet" },
      "extent": { "metaparameter": "n_spike_agecategory" },
      "metadata": { "tags": ["default-db"], "note": "41 rows. The default database's agecategory table, unmodified and read in place.", "esio_format": "parquet" }
    },
    "spike_agegroup": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": { "url_template": "file:///scratch/ctessum/movesdb/movesdb20241112/AgeGroup.parquet" },
      "extent": { "metaparameter": "n_spike_agegroup" },
      "metadata": { "tags": ["default-db"], "note": "7 rows. The default database's agegroup table, unmodified and read in place.", "esio_format": "parquet" }
    }
  },

  "metaparameters": {
    "n_spike_agecategory": {
      "type": "integer", "default": 0,
      "description": "Rows in agecategory. Runtime-discovered by `extent` (docs/esm-conventions.md §11), and the value that closes the child's `spike_agecategory_rows`."
    },
    "n_spike_agegroup": {
      "type": "integer", "default": 0,
      "description": "Rows in agegroup. Closes the child's `spike_agegroup_rows`."
    }
  },

  "index_sets": {
    "spike_agecategory_rows": { "kind": "interval", "size": "n_spike_agecategory" },
    "spike_agegroup_rows": { "kind": "interval", "size": "n_spike_agegroup" }
  },

  "models": {
    "AgeGroupCensus": { "ref": "./age_group_census.esm" }
  }
}
